# The origin of the CDN edge (task 109, ADR 0072 §3, docs/ops/edge.md): the
# second Gcore resource, <prefix2>.gcorecdn.com, pulls this name. Its
# WebSocket /apiws carries the clients' MTProto to the gateway's Edge entry
# (gnetway:11445, on teamgram_net only, never published on the host); the
# rest is the web client, as on PLUMA_WEB_DOMAIN, so that Web K opens through
# the CDN as well.
#
# The Caddyfile imports this file only when PLUMA_EDGE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN is set
# (docker-compose.web.yaml, which refuses to start Caddy without an
# X-Pluma-Edge-Auth value that fits): a site with an empty address would stop
# the whole Caddyfile. The certificate is Let's Encrypt's, as for the other
# names.
#
# - Every request without the right X-Pluma-Edge-Auth, which the Gcore
#   resource adds, is 403 before its path is looked at. The comparison is
#   Caddy's, not one of constant time; the value is 256 random bits, which no
#   one guesses over the network by the time it takes.
# - The gateway takes the client's address from X-Pluma-Client-Addr: the
#   X-Forwarded-For the request came with, whose last element Gcore wrote,
#   the address its edge saw (the gateway takes the last valid address of the
#   list; the elements before it are the client's to forge). Caddy's own
#   X-Forwarded-For, the address of Gcore, is not used: it trusts no proxy.
#   X-Pluma-Edge-Via labels the gateway's metrics; neither header nor the
#   secret passes on as the client sent it.
# - The releases of the client apps (task 115, docs/ops/releases.md): /dl/
#   is the releases service, as on the site, for GET and HEAD only, so that
#   the clients outside the countries of the Russian node download the
#   installers and the updates of the desktop app from Gcore's cache
#   (PLUMA_RELEASES_FILES_URL). The service says how long each answer
#   keeps: a file of a version a year (immutable: it never changes), the
#   lists of releases (releases.json, desktop/current4) no-cache, which
#   Gcore revalidates, the latest links no-store.
# - The pages and files of the web client say no-cache: the resource caches
#   what the origin allows, and Gcore revalidates them by their ETag, so a
#   new version of the web client is seen at once.
# - Nothing else is cached: /apiws, the 403 of a request without the
#   secret, every redirect (a 308 that Caddy's file server answers for a
#   directory once stuck in Gcore's cache) and every error say no-store.
#   304 is not a redirect here: it renews what Gcore holds.
# - No log directive, so no access log; neither Server nor Via in the
#   answers, Caddy's own errors (502 while the gateway is down) included.
{$PLUMA_EDGE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN} {
	@denied not header X-Pluma-Edge-Auth {$PLUMA_EDGE_ORIGIN_AUTH}
	route {
		respond @denied 403
		handle /apiws {
			reverse_proxy gnetway:11445 {
				header_up X-Pluma-Client-Addr {http.request.header.X-Forwarded-For}
				header_up X-Pluma-Edge-Via gcore
				header_up -X-Pluma-Edge-Auth
			}
			header Cache-Control "no-store"
		}
		handle /dl/* {
			@write not method GET HEAD
			respond @write 405
			reverse_proxy releases:9097 {
				header_up -X-Pluma-Edge-Auth
			}
		}
		handle {
			root * /srv
			encode zstd gzip
			header Cache-Control "no-cache"
			file_server
		}
	}
	header {
		X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
		Referrer-Policy no-referrer
		-Server
		-Via
	}
	# After every handler above, the 403 of respond included.
	header {
		Cache-Control "no-store"
		match status 301 302 303 307 308 4xx 5xx
	}
	handle_errors {
		header -Server
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
	}
}
